# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true gives a Windows working tree CRLF copies.
# Git Bash tolerates those, but the same checkout run under WSL/Linux fails with
# "$'\r': command not found" and exits 141 — which for check-bypass-permissions.sh
# is neither of its documented 0/1 exit codes, so a caller misreads the result.
*.sh text eol=lf
